text:
JSON (JavaScript Object Notation)



Raw JSON Structure:
[
  {
    "id": 101,
    "age": 42,
    "sex": "F"
  },
  {
    "id": 102,
    "age": 35,
    "sex": "M"
  }
]



Note


JSON stores data as nested key–value structures: flexible and web-friendly commonly used in modern APIs may require “flattening” into tables

XML (eXtensible Markup Language)



Raw XML Structure:
&lt;participants&gt;
  &lt;participant&gt;
    &lt;id&gt;101&lt;/id&gt;
    &lt;age&gt;42&lt;/age&gt;
    &lt;sex&gt;F&lt;/sex&gt;
  &lt;/participant&gt;
  &lt;participant&gt;
    &lt;id&gt;102&lt;/id&gt;
    &lt;age&gt;35&lt;/age&gt;
    &lt;sex&gt;M&lt;/sex&gt;
  &lt;/participant&gt;
&lt;/participants&gt;



Note



XML organizes data using nested tags
older but still widely used in biomedical and government systems
highly structured and descriptive
commonly seen in legacy APIs and document-based databases
